+## Main push coverage
+
+Every update to `main`, including documentation-only merges and direct pushes,
+runs the full hosted sanitizer matrix and fuzz campaigns at that push's exact
+SHA (#1271). There is no main path filter or no-code qualification exemption.
+Each push has a run-specific concurrency group so rapid merges retain every
+revision's run; only pre-merge PR runs cancel superseded revisions. Do not
+restore a shared main pending slot: disabling in-progress cancellation does
+not prevent pending-run replacement.
+
+Keep post-merge correctness separate from hardware reuse and nightly
+measurements. Main's evidence must remain `scope=full`, `hosted=run` in either
+nightly mode and when a PR's native evidence is reusable. Preserve all
+existing sanitizer configurations/shards and fuzz entries. The selector's
+main-policy mutants, its push fixtures, the evidence glue fixtures in
+`tests/ci/nightly.sh`, and the aggregate's exhaustive self-test pin this
+contract. The [CI guide](../../docs/ci.md#every-update-to-main) records platform
+event restrictions and the distinction from nightly benchmark coverage.
+
